{"agent":"lane-green","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`shas=True` returns before `_tool_mode_refusal`, so flags that the same docstring says are refused, never dropped, are silently ignored. `ddflow_verify(..., id=\"T1\", shas=True, pack_=True, judge_=True)` runs `verify_shas` on `T1` and never refuses the pack/judge combination; `id=\"T1\", phase=\"other\", shas=True` likewise drops `phase` instead of refusing two targets.","digest":"ba533f424b13d1e4","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/verify.py:ddflow_verify","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/verify.py:ddflow_verify"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Landed-path fallback treats any newer commit whose path set merely contains the recorded files as the rewritten landing. Candidates come from `git log -n400` (newest first), and the first commit where `set(landed) <= set(_paths_of(c))` is returned as `rewritten, equivalent <sha> (matched by landed paths)` even when patch-id did not match or the original object is gone. Given a completion whose sha was rebased away and `done.files == [\"src/a.py\"]`, a later typo fix that only touches `src/a.py` is reported as the equivalent of that task, so verify claims the work is on main under the wrong hash.","digest":"3746794d06137cd3","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/verify_shas.py:99 `_equivalent`","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/verify_shas.py:99 `_equivalent`"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":15384,"diff_sha":"d338e1f5506d175c638010942c236c2be9e4793b6279484efd2b4199e5b6ac4e","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/VF-verify-shas","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":90.8,"excluded_bytes":4587,"excluded_files":2,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr"],